The proposed Barber Optimization Algorithm demonstrates excellent optimization performance across all benchmark systems.
Major Outcomes
•	Significant reduction in real power losses. 
•	Improved minimum bus voltage. 
•	Faster convergence compared with conventional metaheuristic algorithms. 
•	Better scalability for large distribution systems. 
•	Stable optimization performance across IEEE 33-, 69-, and 118-bus systems. 
The comparative study confirms that BOA is a reliable optimization technique for Distribution Network Reconfiguration.
